# Migration SQL is checksummed.
#
# Prisma stores a SHA-256 of each migration's bytes in `_prisma_migrations`.
# With core.autocrlf on — the default on Windows — git rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, which changes those bytes and invalidates every hash. The next
# `migrate dev` then reports drift it cannot reconcile and offers one remedy:
# reset the database.
#
# It happened here on a branch switch. Three migrations nobody had touched
# drifted at once, which is a confusing way to learn that a version control
# setting can threaten a production database.
#
# Pinned to LF so the bytes on disk are the bytes that were hashed, on every
# machine.
prisma/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf

# The same for the schema, so a diff is about the schema rather than about
# line endings.
prisma/schema.prisma text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are large and generated; a whole-file CRLF diff is noise.
package-lock.json -text
